adjudication.rationale:
In `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts`, the auth check is:

```ts
if (req.headers[process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME || "calcom-webhook-secret"] !== process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET) {
  return res.status(403)
}
```

If `process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is not set (i.e., `undefined`) and the request does not include the header (so the header lookup is also `undefined`), the comparison becomes `undefined !== undefined`, which is false, so the request is accepted. There is no separate guard requiring the secret to be configured. With `APP_CREDENTIAL_SHARING_ENABLED` true, an unauthenticated caller could then reach the create/update logic and write credentials for an arbitrary `userId`/`appSlug`.
